# Reload the local demo after changes

When a change affects what the user runs locally, do not finish until the running servers have the new code.

- Backend (`backend/`, port 8000): uvicorn `--reload` must log a completed startup after the last edit. If the process is dead or the reload failed, restart it the same way it was already running.
- Next (`app/`, `components/`, `lib/`, port 3000): the dev server must recompile. Restart it if it did not.
- Remotion (`workers/renderer/`): the renderer reads the TypeScript on each Run. No Next restart is required. Already rendered MP4s stay old until a new Run.
- Say so in the reply: servers are on the new code, and a new Run is required when the change is in planning, render or sound. A browser refresh does not replace finished videos.
